mainmenu "ESP-SDR transmit stream over Ethernet"

config APP_TXS_INJECT
	bool "The injector: sample packets made on the board (tx tone, tx inject)"
	help
	  A thread on CPU 0 that makes the packets the sender would, for tests without a host. It costs
	  about 2.4 KB of group 3 (its stack, thread and ring) and a few hundred bytes of group 0, which
	  the network side leaves no room for: injector.conf builds it with two receive buffers less. With
	  it off (the default), the network is the only source and `tx tone` and `tx inject` answer "not
	  supported".

source "Kconfig.zephyr"
